+// format) fails with GL_INVALID_OPERATION and writes nothing, leaving the image's fresh allocation as it was (black, or
+// noise). Those formats are read as RGBA and converted; an image whose read fails is left zeroed (a failed WebGL read
+// writes nothing: the zeroing before it is enough, no glGetError — a synchronous call — on the plain RGBA reads).
